1
00:00:03,324 --> 00:00:05,618
[POLICEMAN 19D]
No! Wait! I did as you said!

2
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:08,037
I killed the criminal
who went after Whiteley!

3
00:00:08,078 --> 00:00:09,580
What more do you want?

4
00:00:09,622 --> 00:00:13,334
Please, spare me!

5
00:00:19,089 --> 00:00:20,341
[HARRY]
Very good.

6
00:00:20,383 --> 00:00:22,176
As per Mister
Milverton's instructions,

7
00:00:22,218 --> 00:00:25,596
we're to make sure that this
officer's body is never found.

8
00:00:25,638 --> 00:00:28,057
Dump him somewhere suitable.

9
00:00:28,098 --> 00:00:30,767
As for our next target...

10
00:00:31,894 --> 00:00:35,981
Heh. The MP's brother,

11
00:00:36,023 --> 00:00:39,235
little Sam Whiteley.

12
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:22,630
[SAM]
What's wrong, Adam?

13
00:02:22,672 --> 00:02:25,090
That's quite the
expression you're wearing.

14
00:02:25,132 --> 00:02:27,343
Something's on
your mind, isn't it?

15
00:02:27,384 --> 00:02:30,137
Yes, a small matter.

16
00:02:30,179 --> 00:02:31,888
But there's no need
to worry, Sam.

17
00:02:31,930 --> 00:02:34,975
Things are going to take
a turn for the better.

18
00:02:35,017 --> 00:02:36,185
Right.

19
00:02:36,226 --> 00:02:38,145
[MAGGIE]
Excuse me, sir.

20
00:02:38,187 --> 00:02:40,981
Chief Inspector Paterson
is here to see you.

21
00:02:41,023 --> 00:02:43,859
[WHITELEY]
All right, I'll be right there.

22
00:02:47,029 --> 00:02:49,657
[SAM] You mean the
world to me brother.

23
00:02:49,699 --> 00:02:52,868
I only wish I could
always be by your side.

24
00:02:55,705 --> 00:02:57,748
[PATERSON]
A few hours ago,

25
00:02:57,790 --> 00:03:00,000
a police officer named
Bartholomew Fowler

26
00:03:00,042 --> 00:03:03,920
was found murdered in
one of the city's slums.

27
00:03:03,962 --> 00:03:05,339
The troubling part

28
00:03:05,381 --> 00:03:10,219
is Officer Fowler was a guard
in the Yard's detention block.

29
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:12,638
The night the bomber was killed,

30
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:15,932
he was the officer on duty.

31
00:03:15,974 --> 00:03:17,476
Per our investigation,

32
00:03:17,518 --> 00:03:21,271
we've discovered Officer Fowler
has a gravely ill mother.

33
00:03:21,313 --> 00:03:24,525
A great deal of money was
required for her care.

34
00:03:24,567 --> 00:03:26,026
Then, two days ago,

35
00:03:26,068 --> 00:03:29,363
he settled with the
hospital in one lump sum.

36
00:03:29,405 --> 00:03:32,408
They got to him by exploiting
the condition of his mother.

37
00:03:32,449 --> 00:03:34,159
Fiends.

38
00:03:34,201 --> 00:03:37,037
So the bomber
was hired to kill me.

39
00:03:37,079 --> 00:03:42,376
Fowler was hired to silence him,
then was silenced himself.

40
00:03:42,418 --> 00:03:43,753
I must also remark.

41
00:03:43,794 --> 00:03:45,087
This extortion and murder

42
00:03:45,128 --> 00:03:48,131
are unlike any of
our previous cases.

43
00:03:48,173 --> 00:03:51,886
This was clearly the
work of a professional.

44
00:03:51,927 --> 00:03:54,930
Listen, please do take
care to be more wary.

45
00:03:54,971 --> 00:03:57,558
We're dealing with
dangerous people.

46
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,393
[WHITELEY]
I understand.

47
00:04:09,194 --> 00:04:12,782
Marcus, kindly cancel
my entire morning schedule.

48
00:04:12,823 --> 00:04:15,284
There's somewhere that
I need to go alone instead.

49
00:04:15,325 --> 00:04:16,493
[MARCUS grunts]

50
00:04:16,535 --> 00:04:19,079
[WHITELEY] Inspector Robinson,
Inspector Sturridge.

51
00:04:19,121 --> 00:04:20,706
I want you to remain
at the residence,

52
00:04:20,748 --> 00:04:22,750
and keep everyone here safe.

53
00:04:22,792 --> 00:04:24,209
After everything
that has happened,

54
00:04:24,251 --> 00:04:25,711
it's simply out of the question!

55
00:04:25,753 --> 00:04:28,380
You heard what the chief
inspector just told you!

56
00:04:28,422 --> 00:04:30,048
Sir, please listen to reason!

57
00:04:30,090 --> 00:04:32,468
I'll be back shortly.
You needn't worry.

58
00:04:32,509 --> 00:04:34,219
But, sir!

59
00:04:45,063 --> 00:04:47,524
He's going to
negotiate by himself.

60
00:04:47,566 --> 00:04:49,735
Awfully bold of him.

61
00:05:05,876 --> 00:05:07,169
[WHITELEY grunts]

62
00:05:07,210 --> 00:05:08,587
Hello there.

63
00:05:08,629 --> 00:05:12,925
My name is Charles
Augustus Milverton.

64
00:05:12,967 --> 00:05:14,844
The House of Lords
requested I act

65
00:05:14,885 --> 00:05:16,929
as their representative.

66
00:05:17,888 --> 00:05:20,390
[MILVERTON] Do you take
any exception to this?

67
00:05:20,432 --> 00:05:22,017
[BONDE]
That's Milverton!

68
00:05:22,058 --> 00:05:23,978
What's he doing here?

69
00:05:24,019 --> 00:05:26,355
I have to let Will
know about this!

70
00:05:27,564 --> 00:05:28,732
No.

71
00:05:28,774 --> 00:05:30,192
Who better to represent them,

72
00:05:30,233 --> 00:05:33,863
than a figure of your
stature and influence.

73
00:05:33,904 --> 00:05:35,113
How kind.

74
00:05:35,155 --> 00:05:37,449
Now, to the matter at hand.

75
00:05:43,873 --> 00:05:45,875
Interesting.

76
00:05:45,916 --> 00:05:48,836
And what do you
intend to do with this?

77
00:05:48,878 --> 00:05:51,672
You'll find my demands
to be rather simple.

78
00:05:51,714 --> 00:05:53,507
For my first concern,

79
00:05:53,549 --> 00:05:56,010
there is a bill I'm pushing
through the House of Commons.

80
00:05:56,051 --> 00:05:57,928
Expanding the vote.

81
00:05:57,970 --> 00:06:01,431
If the House of Lords
fights it, I will go public.

82
00:06:01,473 --> 00:06:02,516
Is that all?

83
00:06:02,558 --> 00:06:04,601
[WHITELEY]
I was getting to that.

84
00:06:04,643 --> 00:06:06,937
No harm will be
visited upon myself,

85
00:06:06,979 --> 00:06:09,064
or any of my family and friends.

86
00:06:09,105 --> 00:06:13,443
Or I swear, I will
go public with this.

87
00:06:13,485 --> 00:06:16,154
But as long as both of
those conditions are met,

88
00:06:16,196 --> 00:06:18,866
I'll bite my tongue.

89
00:06:18,908 --> 00:06:20,659
[MILVERTON]
Hmm.

90
00:06:27,332 --> 00:06:28,417
Very well.

91
00:06:28,458 --> 00:06:30,794
I'll relay both of your
demands to my clients

92
00:06:30,836 --> 00:06:32,963
exactly as you've described.

93
00:06:39,177 --> 00:06:41,805
[WHITELEY] The best
defence is a good offence.

94
00:06:41,847 --> 00:06:46,936
Finally, the path to an ideal
society is all but guaranteed.

95
00:06:46,977 --> 00:06:50,606
[MILVERTON chuckles]
What a farce.

96
00:06:50,647 --> 00:06:54,985
Imagine, me, the king of
blackmailers, being blackmailed.

97
00:06:55,027 --> 00:06:57,237
But unfortunately for him,

98
00:06:57,279 --> 00:07:00,449
I don't back
down under extortion.

99
00:07:11,376 --> 00:07:13,003
[FRED]
What? Someone broke in?

100
00:07:13,045 --> 00:07:13,754
That's impossible!

101
00:07:13,796 --> 00:07:15,422
[GOSLING grunts]

102
00:07:15,464 --> 00:07:16,548
[gasps]

103
00:07:16,590 --> 00:07:19,802
[GOSLING grunts]

104
00:07:19,843 --> 00:07:22,679
[HARRY] Sorry to barge in
when you're in such a rush.

105
00:07:22,721 --> 00:07:24,431
But if you interfere now,

106
00:07:24,473 --> 00:07:27,851
you'll ruin the show
we have all planned out.

107
00:07:27,893 --> 00:07:31,021
We wouldn't want that.

108
00:07:31,063 --> 00:07:34,942
You get to play with us, Fred.

109
00:07:36,485 --> 00:07:38,654
[SAM]
Maggie! Maggie?

110
00:07:38,695 --> 00:07:40,906
I could use your
help with something.

111
00:07:42,908 --> 00:07:44,618
[SAM sighs]

112
00:07:45,452 --> 00:07:49,999
[SAM]
What's the matter? Maggie?

113
00:07:51,207 --> 00:07:54,419
- -[thud]
- -[SAM gasps, groans]

114
00:07:54,461 --> 00:07:56,088
No! Maggie!

115
00:07:56,130 --> 00:07:58,799
[gasps] Oh, my God.

116
00:07:58,841 --> 00:08:01,718
[SAM groans]

117
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:04,429
Thank goodness you're here!
Get a doctor!

118
00:08:04,471 --> 00:08:05,722
Maggie's been--

119
00:08:05,764 --> 00:08:07,641
[SAM gasps]

120
00:08:07,683 --> 00:08:10,435
[thunder rumbles]

121
00:08:17,109 --> 00:08:18,401
[door opens]

122
00:08:18,443 --> 00:08:21,446
[WHITELEY]
Maggie, I made it back.

123
00:08:21,488 --> 00:08:26,702
Hello?

124
00:08:26,743 --> 00:08:29,329
[WHITELEY]
Marcus? Marcus!

125
00:08:29,371 --> 00:08:31,456
What the devil's going on here?

126
00:08:32,708 --> 00:08:34,459
[gasps]

127
00:08:36,086 --> 00:08:38,380
[WHITELEY]
This can't be happening!

128
00:08:38,421 --> 00:08:39,882
[WHITELEY]
No! Samuel!

129
00:08:39,923 --> 00:08:42,634
Please, Maggie!
Someone, answer me!

130
00:08:44,845 --> 00:08:48,098
[WHITELEY]
Wh-What have they done to you?

131
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:49,432
[gasps]

132
00:09:04,364 --> 00:09:05,908
[WHITELEY]
Sam.

133
00:09:05,949 --> 00:09:07,283
[WHITELEY whimpers]

134
00:09:07,325 --> 00:09:12,497
[screams, sobs]

135
00:09:12,539 --> 00:09:14,374
[WHITELEY]
Oh, Sam.

136
00:09:14,416 --> 00:09:16,418
No. Not you.

137
00:09:16,459 --> 00:09:17,460
Why...?

138
00:09:17,502 --> 00:09:22,132
Why? [sobs]

139
00:09:22,174 --> 00:09:22,966
[WHITELEY]
Who's there?

140
00:09:23,008 --> 00:09:24,426
[gasps]

141
00:09:25,677 --> 00:09:27,721
[WHITELEY]
Inspector Sturridge.

142
00:09:27,763 --> 00:09:29,347
Who did this to them?

143
00:09:29,389 --> 00:09:32,768
Why are you the only
one who wasn't killed?

144
00:09:32,809 --> 00:09:35,187
[WHITELEY gasps]
Don't tell me...

145
00:09:35,229 --> 00:09:37,231
[MILVERTON]
The age old question,

146
00:09:37,272 --> 00:09:39,566
why do devils tempt men

147
00:09:39,608 --> 00:09:42,611
to try and sully
their hands with evil?

148
00:09:42,652 --> 00:09:45,114
The answer is remarkably simple.

149
00:09:45,155 --> 00:09:47,783
For a devil compelling
those who do good deeds

150
00:09:47,824 --> 00:09:49,910
to commit despicable acts,

151
00:09:49,952 --> 00:09:52,871
well, there is no
greater pleasure.

152
00:09:52,913 --> 00:09:54,206
Since the dawn of time,

153
00:09:54,248 --> 00:09:59,169
nothing has held more allure
for mankind than wrongdoing.

154
00:09:59,211 --> 00:10:02,714
Consequently, it is depicted
in the Bible as a sin--

155
00:10:02,756 --> 00:10:04,841
a forbidden delight.

156
00:10:04,883 --> 00:10:07,343
The true essence of evil

157
00:10:07,385 --> 00:10:10,139
is the pursuit thereof.

158
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:13,642
When pure, it transcends
the rigors and morals

159
00:10:13,683 --> 00:10:15,685
established by man.

160
00:10:15,727 --> 00:10:18,730
The Lord of Crime's
sins are banal,

161
00:10:18,772 --> 00:10:22,109
merely based on
societal conventions.

162
00:10:22,151 --> 00:10:24,820
Whereas, I, on the other hand--

163
00:10:24,861 --> 00:10:28,949
I am "evil" incarnate.

164
00:10:34,496 --> 00:10:37,166
[WHITELEY]
You're responsible for this?

165
00:10:37,207 --> 00:10:41,044
That's right. It was by my hand.

166
00:10:41,086 --> 00:10:44,923
I killed them,
every member of your family.

167
00:10:44,965 --> 00:10:48,885
[WHITELEY] And you're just
matter-of-factly telling me?

168
00:10:48,927 --> 00:10:50,428
How could you?!

169
00:10:50,470 --> 00:10:54,183
Sam was-- He was nothing
but a defenceless boy.

170
00:10:54,224 --> 00:10:56,143
What reason could
you possibly have?

171
00:10:56,185 --> 00:10:58,520
Why? Why him?

172
00:10:58,561 --> 00:11:01,106
And then you come forward
confessing your sins?

173
00:11:01,148 --> 00:11:03,817
As if you were
seeking absolution?

174
00:11:03,859 --> 00:11:07,362
I have no illusions
about you forgiving me.

175
00:11:07,403 --> 00:11:10,740
However, please believe this.

176
00:11:10,782 --> 00:11:14,661
What I did-- I never wanted
to commit such atrocities.

177
00:11:14,703 --> 00:11:17,080
I don't want to hear
any lies, Sturridge!

178
00:11:17,122 --> 00:11:22,336
I swear, it isn't a lie!
I was forced to under duress!

179
00:11:22,377 --> 00:11:24,296
Explain right now.

180
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:28,091
I don't know who, but someone
took my wife and child,

181
00:11:28,133 --> 00:11:30,677
only leaving behind a threat.

182
00:11:30,719 --> 00:11:33,889
It read "Kill every member
of Whiteley's family.

183
00:11:33,930 --> 00:11:36,683
Then confess what
you've done to him.

184
00:11:36,725 --> 00:11:42,231
Do this and I will return
your wife and child."

185
00:11:43,315 --> 00:11:46,068
[STURRIDGE]
I don't care what happens to me,

186
00:11:46,109 --> 00:11:48,820
as long as my family is safe.

187
00:11:50,155 --> 00:11:52,908
[STURRIDGE]
I killed them with this knife.

188
00:11:52,949 --> 00:11:56,494
Use it. Deliver justice.

189
00:12:04,794 --> 00:12:06,755
[gasps]

190
00:12:06,796 --> 00:12:08,215
[WHITELEY]
This is the man who killed

191
00:12:08,257 --> 00:12:12,719
Sam and Maggie and Marcus.

192
00:12:12,761 --> 00:12:16,390
[grunting]

193
00:12:16,431 --> 00:12:19,726
[grunting]

194
00:12:19,768 --> 00:12:23,479
[WHITELEY growls]

195
00:12:25,565 --> 00:12:27,734
[WHITELEY]
Sam.

196
00:12:27,776 --> 00:12:29,945
Without you in my life,

197
00:12:29,986 --> 00:12:36,618
there's no reason to change the
world, or for me to live in it.

198
00:12:45,668 --> 00:12:50,424
[yells]

199
00:12:50,465 --> 00:12:54,303
[WHITELEY]
Damn! Damn! Damn!

200
00:12:54,344 --> 00:12:59,057
[WHITELEY] I just-- I just
can't bring myself to kill him.

201
00:13:03,437 --> 00:13:05,647
[groans]

202
00:13:20,078 --> 00:13:25,583
[MILVERTON chuckling]

203
00:13:25,625 --> 00:13:29,796
There is no more
satisfactory delight imaginable.

204
00:13:29,838 --> 00:13:34,926
Whiteley, a politician widely
regarded as a hero, uncorrupted,

205
00:13:34,968 --> 00:13:39,514
has just stained his hands
the darkest shade of red.

206
00:13:39,555 --> 00:13:44,519
Yes, exactly as I had intended.

207
00:13:46,271 --> 00:13:50,150
[MILVERTON] And with that,
a new villain emerges.

208
00:13:50,192 --> 00:13:51,860
[clang]

209
00:13:54,863 --> 00:13:57,991
[HARRY laughs] Gotta say,
you're doing remarkably well

210
00:13:58,033 --> 00:13:59,284
for being outnumbered.

211
00:13:59,326 --> 00:14:02,412
I'm beginning to get
invested in this fight.

212
00:14:02,454 --> 00:14:06,291
Sadly, we've got quite
the busy schedule.

213
00:14:06,333 --> 00:14:10,628
Sorry, Fred. Time's up.
Now, you die.

214
00:14:14,257 --> 00:14:15,300
[grunts]

215
00:14:15,342 --> 00:14:16,301
Louis!

216
00:14:16,343 --> 00:14:19,637
I'll handle them! Stay back!

217
00:14:19,679 --> 00:14:21,306
[GOSLING grunts]

218
00:14:24,226 --> 00:14:26,269
I have a message from my boss.

219
00:14:26,311 --> 00:14:29,856
He says, "Let us have a nice
chat about the future sometime,

220
00:14:29,898 --> 00:14:33,402
whilst gazing out over the sea."
You get all that?

221
00:14:33,443 --> 00:14:38,156
We'll continue this later.
I bid you farewell... for now.

222
00:15:03,306 --> 00:15:05,308
[ALBERT]
Mister Whiteley.

223
00:15:07,519 --> 00:15:10,605
[WHITELEY]
Thank you for meeting me here.

224
00:15:10,646 --> 00:15:14,692
I apologize for the hour,
Lord Moriarty.

225
00:15:14,734 --> 00:15:18,447
I thought it'd be best
if I returned the evidence

226
00:15:18,488 --> 00:15:21,741
considering it won't be
of use to me any longer.

227
00:15:23,326 --> 00:15:26,955
I see. And why would that be?

228
00:15:26,996 --> 00:15:30,250
Please keep your composure
when I tell you this,

229
00:15:30,292 --> 00:15:31,960
but earlier tonight,

230
00:15:32,001 --> 00:15:35,630
I killed a man
with my own hands.

231
00:15:35,671 --> 00:15:39,675
My family was slain by
the officer I trusted.

232
00:15:39,717 --> 00:15:44,473
I stabbed him.
I couldn't help myself!

233
00:15:44,514 --> 00:15:46,766
Reasons notwithstanding,

234
00:15:46,808 --> 00:15:50,103
the fact is I took
another man's life.

235
00:15:50,145 --> 00:15:52,897
And a police officer, at that...

236
00:15:52,939 --> 00:15:55,691
I'll be fair game for
my political rivals.

237
00:15:55,733 --> 00:15:58,027
Never mind passing my bill,

238
00:15:58,069 --> 00:16:00,489
the path to bringing
equality to this nation

239
00:16:00,530 --> 00:16:03,825
is completely cut off now.

240
00:16:03,866 --> 00:16:08,704
If only there was a way
I could atone with my own life.

241
00:16:10,999 --> 00:16:12,167
[WILLIAM]
Indeed.

242
00:16:12,208 --> 00:16:15,086
[WHITELEY grunts]
Who are you?

243
00:16:15,128 --> 00:16:19,424
I am Albert's younger brother.
You can call me William.

244
00:16:19,466 --> 00:16:23,261
Younger brother? I didn't
realize that he had one.

245
00:16:23,303 --> 00:16:24,471
Thank you for confessing

246
00:16:24,513 --> 00:16:26,764
despite the deep
grief you're in.

247
00:16:26,806 --> 00:16:31,186
The fact is, you've been setup
by someone, Mister Whiteley.

248
00:16:31,227 --> 00:16:32,479
This individual,

249
00:16:32,521 --> 00:16:35,315
they are attempting to thwart
all efforts of equality

250
00:16:35,357 --> 00:16:38,818
by driving its most vocal
advocate to commit murder.

251
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:39,986
And you did.

252
00:16:40,028 --> 00:16:42,572
Their manipulations
proved successful.

253
00:16:43,948 --> 00:16:46,826
[WHITELEY] Hmph. That's
one way of putting it.

254
00:16:46,868 --> 00:16:48,911
But I'm afraid the
decision to lower myself

255
00:16:48,953 --> 00:16:51,540
and commit murder
was mine alone.

256
00:16:51,581 --> 00:16:54,792
I killed all chances
of reforming Britain.

257
00:16:54,834 --> 00:16:56,836
[WILLIAM]
It's not over just yet.

258
00:16:56,878 --> 00:16:58,880
[WHITELEY grunts]

259
00:16:58,921 --> 00:17:01,466
Sir, if you're truly sincere,

260
00:17:01,508 --> 00:17:04,636
and you intend to atone for
your crime with your death...

261
00:17:06,846 --> 00:17:08,848
...then allow me
to make a request.

262
00:17:08,890 --> 00:17:11,809
Hand your life over to me.

263
00:17:19,234 --> 00:17:23,488
[REPORTERS murmuring]

264
00:17:23,530 --> 00:17:25,407
Seems like there's
a storm brewing.

265
00:17:25,448 --> 00:17:28,993
Just what we need before both
Houses are ready to convene.

266
00:17:29,035 --> 00:17:31,580
I wonder if Whiteley
is really coming after all.

267
00:17:31,621 --> 00:17:35,208
From what I heard, his family
and bodyguards were murdered.

268
00:17:35,250 --> 00:17:39,045
Aye, and even worse than that,
the culprit is still at large.

269
00:17:39,087 --> 00:17:40,880
Look, there he is!

270
00:17:40,922 --> 00:17:42,591
[POLICEMAN 20A]
Everyone, please keep back!

271
00:17:42,632 --> 00:17:44,759
We don't want
anyone in harm's way.

272
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:46,886
You there, keep back!

273
00:17:46,928 --> 00:17:49,180
[REPORTER 20A]
Sir! Mister Whiteley!

274
00:17:49,222 --> 00:17:51,391
Can you describe what you're
going through right now?

275
00:17:51,433 --> 00:17:54,436
[REPORTER 20B] Mister Whiteley!
Your thoughts, please.

276
00:17:54,477 --> 00:17:58,607
I've lost them.
My precious family's gone.

277
00:17:58,648 --> 00:18:00,816
They were murdered
in cold blood,

278
00:18:00,858 --> 00:18:03,861
along with the officers
who were protecting me.

279
00:18:03,903 --> 00:18:08,116
However, I will by no
means take a step back.

280
00:18:08,157 --> 00:18:09,451
You all have my word.

281
00:18:09,492 --> 00:18:12,161
I'll continue fighting
to end inequality.

282
00:18:12,203 --> 00:18:13,496
I won't stop.

283
00:18:13,538 --> 00:18:17,250
No matter if even greater
adversities lie ahead for me.

284
00:18:17,292 --> 00:18:19,294
I won't succumb to fear!

285
00:18:19,335 --> 00:18:25,759
[REPORTERS cheering]

286
00:18:26,509 --> 00:18:31,765
[REPORTERS]
Whiteley! Whiteley! Whiteley!

287
00:18:31,806 --> 00:18:35,644
Whiteley! Whiteley! Whiteley!

288
00:18:35,685 --> 00:18:37,103
[REPORTER 20A]
Mister Whiteley!

289
00:18:37,145 --> 00:18:41,483
You truly are this
country's white knight!

290
00:18:41,524 --> 00:18:42,567
[REPORTERS]
Whiteley!

291
00:18:42,609 --> 00:18:44,778
[thud]

292
00:18:58,166 --> 00:18:59,834
[REPORTERS gasp]

293
00:18:59,875 --> 00:19:02,629
[REPORTER 20B]
Whiteley! He's been stabbed!

294
00:19:08,343 --> 00:19:10,928
Who the devil is that man?

295
00:19:10,970 --> 00:19:12,847
[WILLIAM]
You haven't guessed yet?

296
00:19:12,888 --> 00:19:16,476
I killed the MP's family and the
two inspectors guarding them.

297
00:19:16,518 --> 00:19:18,853
This entire series of
events was orchestrated

298
00:19:18,894 --> 00:19:23,274
and carried out by me,
the Lord of Crime!

299
00:19:23,316 --> 00:19:25,527
Him? He's the one responsible?

300
00:19:25,568 --> 00:19:26,736
It's really him!

301
00:19:26,778 --> 00:19:29,030
I didn't think the
Lord of Crime was real.

302
00:19:29,071 --> 00:19:32,534
Oh, I'm real, and I will
cast all of London society

303
00:19:32,575 --> 00:19:35,119
into the fiery depths of Hell.

304
00:19:35,161 --> 00:19:38,039
That is, unless there's
someone in this city

305
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:40,249
who has what it
takes to stop me!

306
00:19:40,291 --> 00:19:42,711
[REPORTERS gasp]

307
00:19:42,752 --> 00:19:45,963
Seize him! Don't let him go!
We caught him red-handed!

308
00:19:46,005 --> 00:19:46,881
[POLICEMEN]
Sir!

309
00:19:46,922 --> 00:19:48,924
Apprehend the Lord of Crime!

310
00:19:48,966 --> 00:19:51,886
Hold on, sir! We'll get help!

311
00:19:51,927 --> 00:19:55,390
Someone! Fetch a doctor! Hurry!

312
00:19:56,391 --> 00:20:00,729
[WHITELEY] Give my life
to you? How will that help?

313
00:20:00,770 --> 00:20:04,065
[WILLIAM] The class system
is strangling this country.

314
00:20:04,106 --> 00:20:06,818
The people can't
afford to lose hope now,

315
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:09,362
and if your crime
ever comes to light,

316
00:20:09,404 --> 00:20:12,031
then all of their dreams
will turn to despair.

317
00:20:12,073 --> 00:20:14,743
And there will be no
chance at equality.

318
00:20:14,784 --> 00:20:16,118
I agree!

319
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:19,831
But even if I die, it still
won't help to erase my crime!

320
00:20:19,873 --> 00:20:24,419
That's our burden to carry now.
Your crime will become ours.

321
00:20:24,460 --> 00:20:25,754
How can that be?

322
00:20:25,795 --> 00:20:27,171
All I ask is that you die

323
00:20:27,213 --> 00:20:30,425
playing the part of
this country's saviour.

324
00:20:30,466 --> 00:20:34,303
You may consider the performance
to be your final act of penance.

325
00:20:34,345 --> 00:20:37,390
But why? I'm the guilty one!

326
00:20:37,432 --> 00:20:39,475
So why willingly
take the blame for it

327
00:20:39,517 --> 00:20:41,977
and volunteer to
play the villain?

328
00:20:43,145 --> 00:20:44,856
[WILLIAM]
Because...

329
00:20:45,815 --> 00:20:47,400
...that is the role
the Lord of Crime

330
00:20:47,442 --> 00:20:49,944
was always meant to play.

331
00:20:51,905 --> 00:20:52,864
[POLICEMAN 20B]
There he is!

332
00:20:52,906 --> 00:20:55,074
On the roof! Head him off!

333
00:20:55,116 --> 00:20:56,033
[POLICEMEN shout]

334
00:20:56,075 --> 00:20:58,327
Move it! Don't let
the fiend get away!

335
00:20:58,369 --> 00:21:00,455
And cordon off the area!

336
00:21:02,749 --> 00:21:06,419
You've gotta stay
with us, sir! Hold on!

337
00:21:07,545 --> 00:21:09,464
[WHITELEY]
Moriarty.

338
00:21:11,257 --> 00:21:13,092
[WHITELEY]
Without hesitation,

339
00:21:13,134 --> 00:21:15,845
you chose to be
a necessary evil,

340
00:21:15,887 --> 00:21:19,641
the sort this society
desperately needs.

341
00:21:19,682 --> 00:21:22,435
I am sure that you
and your brothers

342
00:21:22,477 --> 00:21:25,939
will be able to bring
change to this nation.

343
00:21:27,523 --> 00:21:29,776
There you are!

344
00:21:36,115 --> 00:21:41,120
[WHITELEY] I leave this land's
fate to you, Lord of Crime.

345
00:21:44,332 --> 00:21:46,626
[WILLIAM]
Which will come out on top?

346
00:21:46,668 --> 00:21:50,004
Necessary evil or pure evil?

347
00:21:50,045 --> 00:21:54,759
In the end only one will
remain. Right, Milverton?

348
00:23:32,523 --> 00:23:35,192
[WATSON] Next time
on Moriarty the Patriot  :

349
00:23:35,234 --> 00:23:37,278
"The Sign of Mary."
